 James Bergin, Erin Kelly, Lev Menand, Thomas Noone, Brett Phillips, Joseph Sommer, Joseph Tracy, Shawei Wang and Jennifer Wolgemuth assisted in preparing these remarks. </p>
  <p><a name="footnote2"></a><sup>2</sup> See Michael Power, <em>The Risk  Management of Everything: Rethinking the Politics of Uncertainty</em> (2004),  37-38 (&ldquo;A functional explanation for the phenomenon suggests that the emergence  of a systematic, generic and broad approach to risk management is a <em>rational</em> response to the fact that the  environment of individuals and organizations, indeed the world, has become  genuinely &lsquo;more risky.&rsquo;&rdquo;).</p>
<p><a name="footnote3"></a><sup>3</sup>
